Negative control for the edit handoff's record id (R-EDIT-HANDOFF, RT2).

A handoff declaring `record: { from: "/id" }` opens its editor on the row's own
record, addressed `.withId(<row id>)` — never `.for(type, id)`. The list surface
reads that pointer off the clicked row and hands the id to the dialog beside the
context. This mutant resolves the pointer and then throws the answer away, so
every Edit opens as if no record were named: the editor boots a fresh draft and
its save would CREATE a link instead of updating the one on the row.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (module lane): list-surface-handoff.spec.ts — an edit handoff with
a `record` pointer must open the dialog with that row's id.

